{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>From righteousness you shall be established.</b> From the hitpa'el binyan, and the tav is swallowed. The sense: that Israel shall do righteousness in the world and not oppress the nations, as is the way of kings." "And the sense of <b>you shall not fear</b>: because of oppression and violence, HaShem will remove the kingdom."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 54, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:31.994383956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}